h coding procedures. By exploiting a general algebraic approach, we show how appropriate encodings of quantum states result in obtaining universal control over dynamically-generated noise-protected subsystems with limited control resources. In particular, we provide an efficient scheme for performing universal encoded quantum computation in a wide class of systems subjected to linear non-Markovian quantum noise and supporting Heisenberg-type internal Hamiltonians.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Dynamical Generation of Noiseless Quantum Subsystems"}], "facet_author_name": ["1948869_Emanuel Knill", "1988640_Lorenza Viola", "1024175_Seth Lloyd"], "core": true, "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2988280", "updated": "2026-02-09T15:02:23.091011"}, "curated": false, "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0002072"}]}, "created": "2025-10-01T10:57:51.059346+00:00", "updated": "2026-02-09T15:02:23.091011+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.85.3520&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}